{"schema":"clawhub.skill.verify.v1","ok":false,"decision":"fail","reasons":["security.status_not_clean"],"slug":"clawquest-agent-mine-openclaw","displayName":"ClawQuest: Agent Mine - OpenClaw Managed Mining","pageUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/zhzai30/skills/clawquest-agent-mine-openclaw","publisherHandle":"zhzai30","publisherDisplayName":"zhzai30","publisherProfileUrl":"https://clawhub.ai/zhzai30","version":"1.0.11","resolvedFrom":"version","tag":null,"createdAt":1777200604529,"card":{"available":true,"path":"skill-card.md","url":"https://wry-manatee-359.convex.site/api/v1/skills/clawquest-agent-mine-openclaw/card?ownerHandle=zhzai30&version=1.0.11","sha256":"f5557af50f02baf0482becbb5c3983bb347b4cde2a1c4bcdc49475c387a5a4fd","size":2488,"contentType":"text/markdown; charset=utf-8"},"artifact":{"sourceFingerprint":"c8a46e11b84e6392487d931256ab4a048ee29257c5d162d50d406b144077a281","bundleFingerprints":["9d2bf1513314d8dc6693e7e4453ed1e0b1f154c2b2e53cfe5dff2c7a9adde37d","bf8d11669d149af4aa8fa306a9a75406136ad5b627ae7d99de336526d0cc6cef"],"files":[{"path":"config/ore-type-map.json","size":1986,"sha256":"2dc93e7d322b98e9f47d46deff72acfc4de458aa5ee55f31787ac7782227578e","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"index.js","size":24780,"sha256":"f3cef8cb0fc800efdf9a47931aef6bd010235ecdf1b88dc8ea576573d16c8313","contentType":"text/javascript"},{"path":"package-lock.json","size":53117,"sha256":"45bdda220db6f646b185fae0f0c0a9f428f09101aa32a03ba2d0413ea34af815","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"package.json","size":267,"sha256":"48a3fb47b39cc7b5df11328c6ba4a086becbf72552d3a487729b0240aec79689","contentType":"application/json"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":8384,"sha256":"abf031ad7e26dc23df64f7b5a8e00dac1a76f531ec51e6ef9e060212881c188c","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"tools.js","size":18489,"sha256":"209c6dc96b0a4ba6a9b636fc82f5766b8b370fdf95bedaafcf304fe5aafa996e","contentType":"text/javascript"}]},"provenance":{"source":"unavailable","reason":"No server-resolved GitHub import provenance is stored for this version."},"security":{"status":"suspicious","passed":false,"rawStatus":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill matches its mining-automation purpose, but it exposes saved game API codes and resource-spending actions through an under-protected local HTTP service.","model":null,"checkedAt":1789540042015,"scannerReports":{"aig":{"version":"2.1.0","$schema":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/oasis-tcs/sarif-spec/main/Schemata/sarif-schema-2.1.0.json","runs":[{"tool":{"driver":{"name":"aig-skill-scan","version":"0.2.1","informationUri":"https://github.com/Tencent/AI-Infra-Guard","rules":[{"id":"T01","name":"Skill Instruction Hijacking","shortDescription":{"text":"Alters the agent's current session goals or safety constraints when the skill is loaded"}},{"id":"T02","name":"Agent Memory Poisoning","shortDescription":{"text":"Writes attacker-controlled rules into persistent memory so they continue to affect future sessions"}},{"id":"T03","name":"Remote Payload Retrieval and Execution","shortDescription":{"text":"Fetches code from an external URL, allowing the effective payload to change after skill review"}},{"id":"T04","name":"Embedded Malicious Code","shortDescription":{"text":"Ships malicious scripts inside the skill package and executes them locally when invoked"}},{"id":"T05","name":"Unauthorized Access and Privilege Escalation","shortDescription":{"text":"Breaks least-privilege boundaries by obtaining permissions beyond the task's legitimate needs"}},{"id":"T06","name":"System Persistence","shortDescription":{"text":"Installs cross-session backdoors, hooks, services, or scheduled tasks that survive the skill run"}},{"id":"T07","name":"Tool Hijacking and Spoofing","shortDescription":{"text":"Modifies, wraps, spoofs, or replaces tools so legitimate-looking calls execute attacker logic"}},{"id":"T08","name":"Insecure Dependencies","shortDescription":{"text":"Introduces malicious packages or components through dependency confusion, typosquatting, or unsafe sources"}},{"id":"T09","name":"Insecure Skill Coding Practices","shortDescription":{"text":"Exposes exploitable flaws such as hardcoded secrets, command injection, plaintext sensitive data, or unsafe temp files"}},{"id":"other","name":"Other Risk","shortDescription":{"text":"Security issues not covered by the T01-T09 classification"}}]}},"results":[{"ruleId":"T05","level":"error","message":{"text":"Unauthenticated Tool API Permits Credential Theft and Unauthorized Game Control"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"index.js"},"region":{"startLine":35,"endLine":36}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"8aa30785eb600cd7"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `index.js:35-36` and `index.js:403-408`  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Missing authentication and authorization  \n**Risk Level**: High\n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```js\napp.post(\"/tool/:name\", async (req, res) => {\n    const parsed = requestSchema.safeParse(req.body ?? {});\n```\n\n```js\nasync function bootstrap() {\n    await loadApiCodeStore();\n    app.listen(port, () => {\n        console.log(`skill-openclaw listening on :${port}`);\n    });\n}\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe common `/tool/:name` handler has no authentication or authorization middleware. Payload validation through Zod only validates request structure; it does not establish the caller's identity or determine whether the caller is authorized to access a cache key or mining session.\n\nIn addition, `app.listen(port)` does not explicitly bind the service to a loopback address. Under Node.js, omitting the host can expose the service on available network interfaces, depending on the deployment environment. Consequently, any client with network access to the listening port can invoke sensitive tools.\n\nThe exposed operations include:\n\n- Reading, replacing, and deleting stored API credentials\n- Purchasing stamina with in-game diamonds\n- Starting managed mining sessions\n- Force-restarting or stopping an existing mining session\n- Reading full mining status and session events\n\nThe optional `cacheKey` is caller-controlled and is not an authorization mechanism. The predictable default value, `default`, further reduces the effort required to access the primary stored credential.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n1. An attacker identifies a reachable deployment of the service on its default TCP port, `4021`, or another configured port.\n2. The attacker sends an unauthenticated request to:\n   ```http\n   POST /tool/get_api_code\n   Content-Type: application/json\n\n   {\"cacheKey\":\"default\"}\n   ```\n3. If a credential has been stored under the default key, the service returns the reusable `apiCode`.\n4. The attacker can then invoke privileged tools such as:\n   - `buy_stamina` to spend in-game diamonds\n   - `start_mining_session` to initiate automated activity\n   - `stop_managed_mining_loop` to disrupt an active session\n   - `start_managed_mining_loop` with `forceRestart: true` to replace another caller's task\n5. The stolen credential can also be reused directly against the upstream game API outside this service.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nAn unauthenticated remote caller can obtain control equivalent to that granted by the victim's game API credential. The resulting scope includes disclosure of the reusable credential, unauthorized consumption of in-game resources, manipulation or interruption of mining operations, and disclosure of mining rewards, player status, and session events.\n\nThe service uses a single global managed-mining task and status object. Therefore, one unauthorized caller can also interfere with the activity and state visible to all other callers using the same service process.\n  ]]>","severity":"High"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Require authentication on every `/tool/:name` endpoint using a strong, independently generated service credential or mutual TLS.\n2. Implement authorization checks that bind each credential, `cacheKey`, mining task, and event stream to an authenticated principal.\n3. Do not treat knowledge of a `cacheKey` or OpenClaw session key as proof of authorization.\n4. Bind to loopback by default:\n   ```js\n   app.listen(port, \"127.0.0.1\", callback);\n   ```\n   Require an explicit configuration change to expose the service remotely.\n5. If remote access is required, place the service behind a TLS-enabled authenticated reverse proxy and enforce network allowlists.\n6. Add rate limiting, request-size limits, audit logging, and alerting for credential-management and resource-purchase operations.\n7. Separate global mining state by authenticated user or tenant to prevent one caller from stopping, restarting, or observing another caller's session.\n8. Require additional confirmation or policy controls for resource-spending operations such as `buy_stamina` and automatic stamina purchases.\n  ]]>"}}]},{"ruleId":"T09","level":"error","message":{"text":"Reusable API Credentials Are Returned and Persisted in Plaintext"},"locations":[{"physicalLocation":{"artifactLocation":{"uri":"index.js"},"region":{"startLine":53,"endLine":59}}}],"partialFingerprints":{"primaryLocationLineHash":"abec5498d954d8fc"},"properties":{"description":"<![CDATA[\n## Vulnerability Details\n**File Location**: `index.js:53-59` and `index.js:431-437`  \n**Vulnerability Type**: Plaintext sensitive-data exposure and insecure secret storage  \n**Risk Level**: High\n\n### Vulnerable Code\n\n```js\nif (toolName === \"get_api_code\") {\n    const cachedApiCode = apiCodeCache.get(cacheKey);\n    if (!cachedApiCode) {\n        return res.status(404).json({ ok: false, error: \"api_code_not_found\" });\n    }\n    return res.json({ ok: true, data: { cacheKey, apiCode: cachedApiCode } });\n}\n```\n\n```js\nasync function persistApiCodeStore() {\n    const apiCodeRecord = Object.fromEntries(apiCodeCache.entries());\n    const serializedStore = JSON.stringify({ apiCodes: apiCodeRecord }, null, 2);\n    await mkdir(path.dirname(apiCodeStorePath), { recursive: true });\n    const tmpPath = `${apiCodeStorePath}.tmp.${process.pid}`;\n    await writeFile(tmpPath, serializedStore, \"utf-8\");\n    await rename(tmpPath, apiCodeStorePath);\n}\n```\n\n### Technical Analysis\n\nThe `get_api_code` tool returns the full reusable game API credential to the caller. This violates secret-minimization principles: callers that only need to know whether a credential is configured receive the secret itself.\n\nThe persistence implementation serializes all credentials as plaintext JSON. The `writeFile` call does not specify a restrictive file mode, so effective permissions depend on the process umask and deployment environment. The temporary file also contains the full plaintext credential before it is renamed.\n\nAlthough the temporary filename includes the process ID, this does not protect its contents from other local users who have filesystem permission to read the directory. The final file and temporary file may therefore expose credentials through filesystem access, backups, snapshots, container volume exports, or accidental artifact collection.\n\nThis weakness is amplified by the absence of authentication on the tool API.\n\n### Attack Path\n\n#### Network exploitation\n\n1. A legitimate user stores an `apiCode` using `set_api_code` or supplies one to another tool, which automatically persists it.\n2. An attacker with network access calls `get_api_code` using the known or guessed cache key.\n3. The response contains the complete reusable `apiCode`.\n4. The attacker reuses the credential to control the account through this service or the upstream game API.\n\n#### Local filesystem exploitation\n\n1. The service writes credentials to the configured `API_CODE_STORE_PATH`, defaulting to `./data/api-code-store.json`.\n2. A local user, compromised process, backup operator, or container-volume reader accesses the plaintext file or its temporary counterpart.\n3. The attacker extracts one or more stored API credentials.\n4. The credentials are reused until revoked or rotated.\n\n### Impact Assessment\n\nExposure of an `apiCode` allows impersonation of the affected game account within the privileges granted by the upstream API. This can include querying account state, controlling mining, collecting rewards, changing automatic-mining state, and spending diamonds on stamina.\n\nBecause all cached credentials are serialized into one record, compromise of the store file may expose every account configured in the service rather than only one cache entry.\n  ]]>","severity":"High"},"fixes":[{"description":{"text":"<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Remove the `get_api_code` operation or change it to return only non-sensitive metadata:\n   ```json\n   {\"cacheKey\":\"default\",\"hasApiCode\":true}\n   ```\n2. Store credentials in an operating-system secret manager, container secret facility, or dedicated encrypted credential service.\n3. If file-based storage is unavoidable:\n   - Create the parent directory with mode `0700`.\n   - Create temporary and final files with mode `0600`.\n   - Verify file ownership and reject symbolic links or unexpected file types.\n   - Keep the store outside web roots, source trees, and shared volumes.\n4. Encrypt credentials at rest with a key held outside the credential file. Restrict access to the decryption key independently.\n5. Authenticate and authorize all credential-management operations.\n6. Redact credentials from responses, logs, diagnostics, backups, and error reports.\n7. Provide credential rotation and revocation procedures, and rotate any credentials that may already have been stored under permissive conditions.\n8. Consider avoiding persistent storage entirely when the credential only needs to exist for the lifetime of a process or authenticated session.\n  ]]>"}}]}],"properties":{"securityScore":20,"primaryLanguage":"JSON","llm":"gpt-5.6","startTime":1789539902.8471012,"endTime":1789539995.4956634}}]},"skillspector":{"skill":{"name":"unknown","source":"/tmp/clawhub-codex-scan-v57a3bma9kn2gkgypvjdj6e97x8eh5pc-ilenxZ/clawscan-skillspector-2020227268/artifact","scanned_at":"2026-09-16T06:24:58.050896+00:00"},"risk_assessment":{"score":98,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","max_issue_severity":"HIGH"},"components":[{"path":"SKILL.md","type":"markdown","lines":218,"executable":false,"size_bytes":8384,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"config/ore-type-map.json","type":"json","lines":76,"executable":false,"size_bytes":1986,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"index.js","type":"javascript","lines":566,"executable":true,"size_bytes":24780,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"package-lock.json","type":"json","lines":1527,"executable":false,"size_bytes":53117,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"package.json","type":"json","lines":16,"executable":false,"size_bytes":267,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null},{"path":"tools.js","type":"javascript","lines":454,"executable":true,"size_bytes":18489,"source_url":null,"source_identity":null,"source_digest":null}],"structured_summaries":[],"issues":[{"id":"AE1","finding_id":"finding-ffe7ec461f914346a745a16ec7475415","category":"analysis-evasion","pattern":null,"severity":"HIGH","confidence":1,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":25,"end_line":null},"finding":"SKILL.md (partial)","explanation":"Referenced artifact was not completely inspected","remediation":"Make the referenced artifact locally available and fully analyzable, or remove the reference.","code_snippet":"runtime code to “fix” behaviour. Use documented environment variables and this `SKILL.md` only.","intent":null,"tags":["coverage","reference","target-disposition:partial"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"3759e6a4effbd89fa5b6fc80754a6923d55bc99fda186e8e597107f2cd346b04","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":25,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"RA1","finding_id":"finding-5f5fb9b9375c4fb19aff59d584afb6f7","category":"Rogue Agent","pattern":"Self-Modification","severity":"HIGH","confidence":0.85,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":26,"end_line":null},"finding":"write Skill","explanation":"Skill modifies its own code, configuration, or behavior at runtime. Self-modification enables an agent to escalate privileges, disable safety constraints, or install persistent backdoors.","remediation":"Prevent the skill from modifying its own code, SKILL.md, or configuration files. Treat skill files as read-only at runtime.","code_snippet":"\n- **Tools only**: Interact with the game **only** through this Skill’s **tool** HTTP API — `POST /tool/:name` on the skill-openclaw service, using the tool names documented below (`set_api_code`, `check_mining_state`, `start_managed_mining_loop`, etc.). Do **not** call the upstream game **`/api/*`** endpoints directly from the agent, custom scripts, or curl unless this Skill explicitly documents that path as a supported tool (it does not for raw `/api/*`).\n- **Do not modify source**: Do **not** edit, patch, or fork the `skill-openclaw` source tree, `package.json`, or runtime code to “fix” behaviour. Use documented environment variables and this `SKILL.md` only.\n- **Report errors; do not self-heal in code**: If a tool fails or behaviour is unexpected, **report** the failure (HTTP status, response body, tool name, `cacheKey`, timestamps, logs). Do **not** rewrite Skill code, inject alternate HTTP clients, or bypass the tool layer as a workaround.\n\n## API Contract\n","intent":null,"tags":["Rogue Agent","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"d3d1df715fa69a79750b2e473493c486f496d697ec663eb03cf4b3890ebb121a","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":26,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-0312271fdf10400290581c0b983e3099","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":72,"end_line":77},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill explicitly documents persisting an `apiCode` for later reuse and even exposes a default file path for the credential store, but it does not warn users that this is a sensitive authentication secret or describe storage protections. If the local filesystem, logs, backups, or shared runtime are accessible, the cached `apiCode` could be recovered and used to control the user's game account actions through the authenticated API.","remediation":"Document `apiCode` as a secret, warn users that it is stored locally, and describe the security implications of persistence. Prefer secure secret storage over plaintext files, restrict file permissions, avoid logging the token, support opt-out/ephemeral mode by default, and add guidance for rotating/revoking compromised `apiCode` values.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":72,"end_line":77}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-769f2b35300e4a0aaa72edbb367b708d","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":122,"end_line":145},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill supports `buy_stamina` and `autoBuyStamina` behavior that automatically spends diamonds, but the documentation does not clearly warn that enabling this feature can consume in-game currency without per-purchase confirmation. In an automated loop, this can lead to unintended repeated spending and user loss, especially if defaults or retries are misunderstood.","remediation":"Add explicit warnings anywhere `buy_stamina` or `autoBuyStamina` is documented, stating that diamonds/in-game currency will be spent automatically. Require explicit opt-in, recommend conservative limits, expose spending caps/dry-run options, and document how to disable or stop automatic purchases quickly.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":122,"end_line":145}]},{"id":"P9","finding_id":"finding-843666c525be4948a7572fc33d3bf491","category":"Prompt Injection","pattern":"Whitespace Padding","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":197,"end_line":null},"finding":"U+0020 x106","explanation":"Large whitespace padding was detected (a block of blank lines or a long run of spaces). This can push injected instructions below or to the right of the visible area so a human reviewer never sees them while the agent still reads them. Manual review of the hidden content is recommended.","remediation":"Remove the large whitespace padding (blank-line blocks or long space runs) and review any content hidden below or to the right of it. Keep skill files compact and reviewable so no instructions can be concealed off-screen.","code_snippet":"\n### Mining Errors\n\n| Code | Name                  | Description                                                                                                          |\n| ---- | --------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 2003 | InsufficientResources | Insufficient stamina to start mining                                                                                 |\n| 2008 | DiamondNotEnought     | Insufficient diamonds                                                                                                |","intent":null,"tags":["Prompt Injection","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"d044f8a1d0b254e8ba794a1e51ee0e9cfe9943e075d293b017dd36bf6207e310","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":197,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"P9","finding_id":"finding-a3029e298d36444fa71608e98398c409","category":"Prompt Injection","pattern":"Whitespace Padding","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":199,"end_line":null},"finding":"U+0020 x81","explanation":"Large whitespace padding was detected (a block of blank lines or a long run of spaces). This can push injected instructions below or to the right of the visible area so a human reviewer never sees them while the agent still reads them. Manual review of the hidden content is recommended.","remediation":"Remove the large whitespace padding (blank-line blocks or long space runs) and review any content hidden below or to the right of it. Keep skill files compact and reviewable so no instructions can be concealed off-screen.","code_snippet":"\n| Code | Name                  | Description                                                                                                          |\n| ---- | --------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 2003 | InsufficientResources | Insufficient stamina to start mining                                                                                 |\n| 2008 | DiamondNotEnought     | Insufficient diamonds                                                                                                |\n| 2009 | MiningStateConflict   | Mining state conflict (e.g. calling `startMining` while already in progress, or `endMining` when not mining via API) |\n| 2014 | MiningApiNotActive    | API mining feature not activated for this player                                                                     |","intent":null,"tags":["Prompt Injection","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"54d72fc3e34aa74963c96340428a41131bc74bfc2bbb7589df844519a9bfadff","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":199,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"P9","finding_id":"finding-73ab4387457a4f8c85b15c786b52bdb1","category":"Prompt Injection","pattern":"Whitespace Padding","severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.7,"location":{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":200,"end_line":null},"finding":"U+0020 x96","explanation":"Large whitespace padding was detected (a block of blank lines or a long run of spaces). This can push injected instructions below or to the right of the visible area so a human reviewer never sees them while the agent still reads them. Manual review of the hidden content is recommended.","remediation":"Remove the large whitespace padding (blank-line blocks or long space runs) and review any content hidden below or to the right of it. Keep skill files compact and reviewable so no instructions can be concealed off-screen.","code_snippet":"| Code | Name                  | Description                                                                                                          |\n| ---- | --------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n| 2003 | InsufficientResources | Insufficient stamina to start mining                                                                                 |\n| 2008 | DiamondNotEnought     | Insufficient diamonds                                                                                                |\n| 2009 | MiningStateConflict   | Mining state conflict (e.g. calling `startMining` while already in progress, or `endMining` when not mining via API) |\n| 2014 | MiningApiNotActive    | API mining feature not activated for this player                                                                     |\n| 2018 | MiningNotFinished     | Mining not finished yet (current time has not reached `estimatedEndAt`)                                              |","intent":null,"tags":["Prompt Injection","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"49a51872da3d60d7b5037d8645fc1567cc7e0cb864667db46cc3d16f5075c7de","occurrences":[{"file":"SKILL.md","start_line":200,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-d501e8b985024e05a3a1916eca7f3f73","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.81,"location":{"file":"index.js","start_line":26,"end_line":27},"finding":null,"explanation":"The skill uses `API_CODE_STORE_PATH` to determine where API codes are persisted, which directly affects storage of sensitive credentials on the host filesystem. There is no visible warning in this file informing users or operators that credentials are stored locally at a configurable path.","remediation":"Add a clear warning in comments, logs, or documentation that API codes are written to a local file path controlled by `API_CODE_STORE_PATH`, and provide guidance for securing that file location.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"index.js","start_line":26,"end_line":27}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-720cfcdcd83a47e2abf87060101a42fa","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"index.js","start_line":49,"end_line":50},"finding":null,"explanation":"The service persists user-supplied API codes to a JSON file on disk, creating a durable credential store without any access control, encryption, or minimization shown in this file. If the host filesystem, backups, logs, or container volumes are exposed, attackers can recover valid API credentials and act as users against the upstream game API.","remediation":"Do not persist API codes by default; keep them in memory only unless explicit secure storage is required. If persistence is necessary, encrypt secrets at rest with a managed key, restrict filesystem permissions, add retention/expiry, and clearly document/disclose that credentials are being stored.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"index.js","start_line":49,"end_line":50}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-52a6dfe5734e44e2aab6383792c12153","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.98,"location":{"file":"index.js","start_line":53,"end_line":58},"finding":null,"explanation":"The get_api_code endpoint returns the full cached API code to any caller who knows or can guess the cacheKey, and this file shows no authentication or authorization checks. Because the default cache key is predictable (\"default\"), this effectively exposes stored credentials over HTTP and enables account takeover or unauthorized API actions.","remediation":"Remove the ability to return raw stored API codes, or replace it with a boolean presence check/redacted metadata only. Require strong authentication and per-user authorization for all credential operations, and avoid predictable shared cache keys such as \"default\".","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"index.js","start_line":53,"end_line":58}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-9e01392d09c84fefaabf8d9944ede278","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.84,"location":{"file":"index.js","start_line":153,"end_line":156},"finding":null,"explanation":"The code records openclawSessionKey into managed mining session events and later exposes session events through a status endpoint, causing session-associated secret material to be retained and retrievable. Even if this is an internal session identifier, storing and returning it broadens exposure through API consumers, memory dumps, logs, and debugging interfaces.","remediation":"Do not store raw session keys in event payloads or status objects; redact or hash them if correlation is needed. Limit event data to non-sensitive metadata, and gate status/event endpoints behind authentication with least-privilege access.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"index.js","start_line":153,"end_line":156}]},{"id":"SQP-3","finding_id":"finding-71b86a6faee543d5a7b3b311ba6fa638","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.95,"location":{"file":"tools.js","start_line":11,"end_line":19},"finding":null,"explanation":"The file sets zh_CN as the default language and normalizeLanguage falls back to that locale whenever the provided language is unsupported or missing. This forces a specific language choice without explicit user opt-in, which violates the language/locale policy described in the audit rules.","remediation":"Require an explicit user language selection, preserve the caller's locale where possible, or document and justify the default locale behavior with a clear opt-in or configuration mechanism.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"tools.js","start_line":11,"end_line":19}]},{"id":"SQP-2","finding_id":"finding-52c8bd7c6a6948f48f09ad7be98399c7","category":null,"pattern":null,"severity":"MEDIUM","confidence":0.92,"location":{"file":"tools.js","start_line":93,"end_line":122},"finding":null,"explanation":"The code automatically attempts to spend in-game premium currency (diamonds) via /api/buyStamina after detecting insufficient stamina, with no built-in confirmation, budget cap, explicit user-consent record, or warning at the point of purchase. In an agent/automation context, this can cause unintended resource depletion or real-money-equivalent loss if enabled by configuration or invoked without the operator fully understanding the side effect.","remediation":"Require explicit opt-in before any purchase action and add a hard confirmation/control layer outside the retry loop. Implement spend limits, dry-run/preview mode, audit logging, and a configurable maximum total purchases or diamond budget; default auto-buy to disabled and require clear user-visible disclosure when enabling it.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":[],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":null,"occurrences":[{"file":"tools.js","start_line":93,"end_line":122}]},{"id":"SC4","finding_id":"finding-9758e7f3b19b43528ff7ce464f7f6213","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Known Vulnerable Dependency: body-parser==1.20.4 — 1 advisory(ies): CVE-2026-12590 (body-parser vulnerable to denial of service when invalid limit value silently di)","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.94,"location":{"file":"package-lock.json","start_line":603,"end_line":null},"finding":"body-parser==1.20.4","explanation":"The lockfile includes body-parser 1.20.4 as a production dependency through Express. If the referenced advisory is valid, a remotely triggerable denial of service in request body parsing is applicable to a network-facing agent because malformed requests can reach this code path and consume resources or crash request handling.","remediation":"Upgrade to a patched body-parser release, or upgrade Express to a version that pulls in the fixed transitive dependency. In addition, enforce strict request size/type limits and add tests for malformed limit/body inputs to verify the parser fails safely.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"43e9a17d30e35f359c83ff7f5cf5158137373008759cfcafee26f0545b595535","occurrences":[{"file":"package-lock.json","start_line":603,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC4","finding_id":"finding-5321bf29e3784d34b19c41c51ca9e57a","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Known Vulnerable Dependency: esbuild==0.27.7 — 1 advisory(ies): GHSA-g7r4-m6w7-qqqr (esbuild allows arbitrary file read when running the development server on Window)","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.6,"location":{"file":"package-lock.json","start_line":788,"end_line":null},"finding":"esbuild==0.27.7","explanation":"Dependency has known vulnerabilities (CVEs). Using packages with unpatched security flaws exposes the environment to known exploits.","remediation":"Update the dependency to a patched version that addresses the known CVE. Check OSV (osv.dev) or NVD for details on the vulnerability.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain","llm-unconfirmed"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"d89352dbbdcd4f99e1cdf3a666b8c0dde79b98366610bb9940e9b53d09e92f34","occurrences":[{"file":"package-lock.json","start_line":788,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC4","finding_id":"finding-1782d968f1ab4d42a0f40403393fc377","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Known Vulnerable Dependency: qs==6.14.2 — 3 advisory(ies): CVE-2026-82417 (qs: Denial of Service via Attacker Controlled isBuffer); CVE-2026-8723 (qs has a remotely triggerable DoS: qs.stringify crashes with TypeError on null/u); CVE-2026-82562 (qs array-limit bypass via bracket-key comma parsing)","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.91,"location":{"file":"package-lock.json","start_line":1220,"end_line":null},"finding":"qs==6.14.2","explanation":"The lockfile includes qs 6.14.2 as a production dependency through Express/body-parser. Since qs commonly parses attacker-controlled query strings or urlencoded bodies in HTTP services, reported DoS flaws are relevant in this context and could let an external client trigger excessive processing or parser failures.","remediation":"Upgrade qs to a patched version, directly or by upgrading Express/body-parser to versions that resolve the transitive dependency. Also constrain query/body parser depth, parameter count, and overall request size, and reject unusually complex nested inputs at the edge.","code_snippet":null,"intent":null,"tags":["Supply Chain"],"evidence":{},"match_fingerprint":"ca0df11739b5d46193a7d507201372eb845d59ff78a8ad30666c8df3a072b497","occurrences":[{"file":"package-lock.json","start_line":1220,"end_line":null}]},{"id":"SC1","finding_id":"finding-1b40660232874ea49518e3c0bb26cd52","category":"Supply Chain","pattern":"Unpinned Dependencies","severity":"LOW","confidence":0.4,"location":{"file":"package.json","start_line":10,"end_line":null},"finding":"\"express\": \"^4.21.2\"","explanation":"Dependencies lack version pinning, allowing potential maliciou